        "answer": {
          "short": "i $y=x+1$; ii $y=2x$; iii $y=-\\frac12x+\\frac52$; iv $y=2$. See the shared graph.",
          "worked": "Substitute each value of $m$:\n$$\\begin{align*}\\text{i}\\quad y-2&=x-1\\\\y&=x+1\\\\\\text{ii}\\quad y-2&=2(x-1)\\\\y&=2x\\\\\\text{iii}\\quad y-2&=-\\tfrac12(x-1)\\\\y&=-\\tfrac12x+\\tfrac52\\\\\\text{iv}\\quad y-2&=0\\\\y&=2.\\end{align*}$$\nFor i, plot $(-1,0)$ and $(0,1)$. For ii, plot $(0,0)$ and $(1,2)$. For iii, plot $(5,0)$ and $(0,\\frac52)$. For iv, draw the horizontal line through $(0,2)$. Extend each line in both directions on the same axes.",
          "solutionDiagrams": [
