        "id": "p19-q14-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "Prove that the line $y-2=m(x-1)$ passes through the point found in the previous part, regardless of the value of $m$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "At $(1,2)$, $y-2=0$ and $m(x-1)=m(0)=0$ for every $m$, so the point always lies on the line.",
          "worked": "Substitute $x=1$:\n$$\\begin{align*}y-2&=m(1-1)\\\\y-2&=0\\\\y&=2.\\end{align*}$$\nThus $(1,2)$ satisfies the equation for every value of $m$.",
